Every file in this folder, plus ../x86_64-ps5-freebsd.json and ../prepare-rust-std.py, is copied
unchanged from PS5 Dump Forge (GPL-3.0-or-later):

  https://github.com/quer3q/ps5-dump-forge  commit 8295556 (2026-11)
  ps5/shim/*, ps5/x86_64-ps5-freebsd.json, ps5/prepare-rust-std.py

which copied them unchanged from ps5-ai-cli (GPL-3.0-or-later):

  https://github.com/saawant12/ps5-ai-cli  commit eb1d494 (2026-10-04)
  platform/{freebsd11.c, its #included .c files, compat.h, syscalls.S, syscalls.link}
  targets/x86_64-ps5-freebsd.json, tools/prepare-rust-std.py

ps5-ai-cli verified this set on a PS5 at firmware 13.60 (Rust std: threads, files, Tokio), and
Forge ships it. Keep it byte-identical (payload/convert/build.sh checks the hashes below); carry
our own changes in ../entry.c, ../compat.c and ../linker.sh.

../compat.c is Forge's ps5/compat.c, unchanged (statfs symbol versions, the CPU-count answer).
../linker.sh, ../Dockerfile and ../build.sh are adapted from Forge's ps5/ files of the same names.

